    "done_when": "tests/test_control_is_compared_with_the_head_arm.py builds manifests plus logs in a temporary run directory for five cases, each calling the promotion gate's control check: (a) test-first: the control's failing id is red in baseline_suite, green in after_suite, so the control is admitted; (b) the control's only failing id also fails in after_suite, so it is refused; (c) no readable after_suite, so the baseline comparison decides as today (admitted when the id is absent from baseline, refused when present); (d) a control log with EXIT=0 is refused; (e) a control log with no EXIT= line is refused as today. Case (a) fails at the base revision (logged) and passes at the head. A replay section in the manifest runs the new check read-only against the four named runs' real manifests and control logs, recording that each is now admitted, without writing to those run directories. The negative control, in a scratch copy, restores the baseline-only comparison; case (a) fails, with the mutation on the red log's first line and an EXIT= line after pytest's output. The gate is the new test plus every tests/ file whose name contains negative_control or control_gate; both arms are recorded as one JSON object each under baseline_suite and after_suite (revision, command, exit_status, one log_path, failure_ids), each log ending in an EXIT= line, with the head arm adding no failing id. ruff check plus ruff format --check on the changed paths add no finding against the base. The tests neither read nor write the real ~/.config/reckon.",
    "estimated_hours": null,
    "goal": "Plan crew-runtime-positive-controls, followup f-crpc-a-test-first-baseline-refuses-a-sound-control: the negative-control gate admits a control that reddens a test the head arm passes. Read the followup in docs/plans/crew-runtime-positive-controls.html, including reckon-d5's added instance. _require_declared_negative_control in reckon/crew/promotion.py (near :4850) admits a control only when it fails an id the baseline arm does not fail (baseline_failure_ids near :4948). A node whose tests are written first has every new case red at base by design, so a sound control on one of them is refused; four promotions on 2026-09-28 needed a waiver for exactly this (runs r-20260928T142644163914, r-20260928T193532461213, r-20260928T204215455574, r-20260929T001417713998). Make the admitting fact: the control exits non-zero with at least one failing id that the head arm (after_suite) passes, falling back to the baseline comparison only when the manifest records no readable head arm.",
